+# Ellipse tutorial and Starter Circuit removal — 2026-10-25
+
+The first tutorial race now uses the existing **Ellipse** layout for all five laps. Ellipse is also the only native fallback track. Its original official creator document, start line and 28 tyre objects are preserved; the tutorial keeps the touch highlights and corrected parking-stop behavior.
+
+| Requirement | Delivered change |
+| --- | --- |
+| TE01 | Precompiled `resources/tracks/ellipse.json` comes from the existing bundled official Ellipse document, `track_954fdea809f4a6b7`, with no layout edits. The ready card names Ellipse, and the tutorial opens that native document offline. Countdown, five ordered laps, local PB, retry, account fences and exact-document lesson authority remain. |
+| TE02 | Delete the Starter Circuit native asset, its install-time cloud copy, and both obsolete generation/export scripts and UIDs. Replace its native catalogue entry with Ellipse. Remove it from the local backend seed catalogue and bundled hash index, leaving 26 documents. Existing last-track preferences fall back safely; old player files/preferences and historical evidence remain. |
+| TE03 | `scripts/dev.ps1 GenerateEllipse` reproducibly prepares the existing Ellipse; remove `GenerateStarter` and `GenerateBackendStarter`. Standalone verifier packaging copies Ellipse. Active diagnostics/tests load the replacement resource, and current player/developer guides name it. |
+| R01 / G01 / Q01 | Preserve exact before snapshots, native screenshots, commands, failures, final source hashes and an isolated Git-checked task patch. Preserve concurrent work and owner processes. |
+
+The public Ellipse creator document and every remaining installed cloud document keep their exact bytes and content hashes. Only the precompiled local wrapper has native identity `ellipse`. Tutorial access still requires that exact in-memory document and the current account scope; it grants no publication or online verification authority.
+
+The focused harness checks the Ellipse identity and exact original creator document, absence of the retired asset, touch input, actual parking objectives, all five race laps, PB/retry, persistence and account/invitation fences. Ellipse's tyre wall blocks the simple centreline regression driver, so the harness uses the existing development `ProfiledRouteDriver` with obstacle detours. It still supplies ordinary quantized inputs to the real Game and simulation; no poses, checkpoint counts, times or results are fabricated. A centreline trajectory is built directly because the detour controller does not need pilot optimisation. The successful race uses 7,116 simulation ticks.
+
+The editor regression now waits for pending commits, native collision and visible-world preparation before testing gestures. Its original paint, history, cancellation and remix assertions remain. This corrects test timing around the existing input gate; no editor runtime behavior is changed.
+
+See [the machine report](evidence/tutorial-ellipse-2026-10-25/report.json), [native gallery](evidence/tutorial-ellipse-2026-10-25/report.html) and [task-only checkpoint](evidence/tutorial-ellipse-2026-10-25/task-only.patch) for exact results, commands and hashes. All tests use pinned Godot 4.7.2 via `scripts/dev.ps1`, disposable workspace-local APPDATA and local fixtures. Backend checks use the configured secure Python environment, temporary SQLite databases and packaged local verifier projects.
+
+Retained attempts include the centreline driver's collision with Ellipse's tyres; five then one editor assertions before the preparation/commit waits were corrected; and a standalone verifier fixture expecting physics 0.66 while concurrent runtime work used 0.67. The fixture was subsequently updated by concurrent work, and the unchanged verifier test passes on recheck. A Mobile launch also encountered a missing `electric_coachwork.gd` during an unrelated car-model edit; the completed retry passes. A retirement rerun with reused test userdata failed its empty-publications check; the fixture now disables the API before startup and its retained fresh-userdata run passes without changing that assertion. System Python lacked pytest; backend checks use `.tools/backend-secure-venv`.
+
+Reload the client to load the new resource catalogue. **Settings → Help → Replay tutorial** opens the updated lesson. No physical device check/test, APK, deployment, live server/player mutation, purchase or owner-process restart is performed. Existing server publications require their normal separate lifecycle operation; changing local bundle/seed inputs does not delete live publications or historical race data.
